{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghWmq1caUHwbM55udFae","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The high-spin to low-spin crossover happens at **Dq ≈ 1 792 cm⁻¹** (10Dq ≈ 17 920 cm⁻¹). At this point the ground state changes from ⁶A₁g (t₂g³e_g²) to ²T₂g (t₂g⁵).\n\n**Method**\nI set up the full d⁵ problem in the 252-determinant basis. The Racah parameters were converted to Slater integrals (F₄ = C/35, F₂ = B + 5F₄), and the octahedral crystal field was included in units of Dq. I then searched for the Dq at which the lowest doublet has the same energy as the sextet, using B = 621 cm⁻¹ and C = 2 851 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Results**\n1. **⁶A₁g energy:** this state comes only from the t₂g³e_g² configuration, so its energy, −35B, does not change with Dq.\n2. **Simple estimate (one configuration only):** treating ²T₂g as pure t₂g⁵ gives E = −20Dq − 20B + 10C. Setting this equal to −35B gives 20Dq = 15B + 10C, so Dq ≈ 1 891 cm⁻¹.\n3. **Full calculation:** in the full calculation, ²T₂g also mixes with ²T₂g terms from other configurations (configuration interaction). This lowers its energy, so the crossing comes earlier, at **Dq = 1 791.8 cm⁻¹**. At that value the lowest ⁴T₁g state is still about 5 000 cm⁻¹ higher, so it is never the ground state.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1792, \"B\": 621, \"C\": 2851, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Full d5 diagonalization gives the 6A1g/2T2g ground-state crossover at Dq of about 1792 cm^-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1869,"cache_read_input_tokens":4100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1869,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6132eaf3-ac66-4d70-ae78-b15449891507","uuid":"f3e5923